From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250: vote the top DDR level from 650 MHz up

0110's stock votes ask for 8171875 kBps (DDR at 2092 MHz) from 587 MHz
up, though the memory runs up to 2736 MHz (10944000 kBps, the top of the
LLCC bandwidth monitor's table). Vote the top DDR level from 650 MHz up
(670 is kettle-powerd's automatic ceiling on the RP5, and 0111's
overclock OPPs go to 750).

Skyrim SE on an RP5, same spot, 60 s each: at 670 MHz 24.3 fps with the
stock vote, 25.6 with the top one; at 587 MHz no change (23.7 / 23.6),
so 587 keeps its stock vote. The vote still drops with the GPU when it
runtime-suspends.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
@@ -2981,7 +2981,7 @@
 					opp-level = <RPMH_REGULATOR_LEVEL_TURBO_L1>;
 					opp-supported-hw = <0xb>;
 					qcom,opp-acd-level = <0x802b5ffd>;
-					opp-peak-kBps = <8171875>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <10944000>;
 				};
 
 				opp-725000000 {
@@ -2989,7 +2989,7 @@
 					opp-level = <RPMH_REGULATOR_LEVEL_TURBO_L1>;
 					opp-supported-hw = <0xb>;
 					qcom,opp-acd-level = <0x802b5ffd>;
-					opp-peak-kBps = <8171875>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <10944000>;
 				};
 
 				opp-700000000 {
@@ -2997,7 +2997,7 @@
 					opp-level = <RPMH_REGULATOR_LEVEL_TURBO>;
 					opp-supported-hw = <0xb>;
 					qcom,opp-acd-level = <0x802b5ffd>;
-					opp-peak-kBps = <8171875>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <10944000>;
 				};
 
 				opp-670000000 {
@@ -3005,7 +3005,7 @@
 					opp-level = <RPMH_REGULATOR_LEVEL_NOM_L1>;
 					opp-supported-hw = <0xb>;
 					qcom,opp-acd-level = <0x802b5ffd>;
-					opp-peak-kBps = <8171875>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <10944000>;
 				};
 
 				opp-650000000 {
@@ -3013,7 +3013,7 @@
 					opp-level = <RPMH_REGULATOR_LEVEL_NOM_L1>;
 					opp-supported-hw = <0xb>;
 					qcom,opp-acd-level = <0x802b5ffd>;
-					opp-peak-kBps = <8171875>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <10944000>;
